    <DataNode elementId="AT3G54470-MONOMER" textLabel="orotate phosphoribosyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q42586" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding the bi-functional UMP synthase expressing orotate phosphoribosyltransferase and orotidine-5&apos;-phosphate decarboxylase activity catalyzing the fifth and sixth step in the &lt;i&gt;de novo&lt;/i&gt; pyrimidine ribonucleotide biosynthesis has been isolated and partly functionally characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. Its molecular function(s) of both forming orotidine-5&apos;-monophosphate (OMP) using PRPP and decarboxylating OMP to UMP in the final step has been demonstrated by functionally complementing auxotrophic yeast mutants deficient in both activities |CITS: [8041358]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G54470-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G54470.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smart" value="SM00934" />
