    <DataNode elementId="AT3G20330-MONOMER" textLabel="AT3G20330-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P49077" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding aspartate carbamoyltransferase in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; has been isolated and partly functionally characterized. Its molecular function of N-carbamoyl-L-aspartate from aspartate and carbamoyl-phosphate has been demonstrated by functionally complementing a auxotrophic yeast mutant deficient in the aspartate carbamoyltransferase activity |CITS: [8041358]|.</Comment>
